solution_steps:
We can use long division to divide $x^3$ by $x^2 + 5x + 1$:
$$
\begin{array}{c|cc cc}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{x} & -5 & + \frac{25}{x+5} \\
\cline{2-5}
x^2 + 5x + 1 & x^3 & & & \\
\multicolumn{2}{r}{-x^3} & -5x^2 & -x^2 & \\
\cline{2-4}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{0} & -5x^2 & -x^2 & \\
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & +5x^2 & +25x & +5 \\
\cline{3-5}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & & 24x & +5 \\
\end{array}
$$
Therefore, the remainder when $x^3$ is divided by $x^2 + 5x + 1$ is $\boxed{24x + 5}$.The answer is: 24x+5

