The product of two matrices is found by multiplying corresponding entries and adding the results.
We have \[
\begin{pmatrix} 2 & 3 \\ 7 & -1 \end{pmatrix}
\begin{pmatrix} 1 & -5 \\ 0 & 4 \end{pmatrix}
=
\begin{pmatrix} (2)(1)+(3)(0) & (2)(-5)+(3)(4) \\ (7)(1)+(-1)(0) & (7)(-5)+(-1)(4) \end{pmatrix}
=
\begin{pmatrix} 2 & 2 \\ 7 & -39 \end{pmatrix}.
\]
So the product is $\boxed{\begin{pmatrix} 2 & 2 \\ 7 & -39 \end{pmatrix}}$.The answer is: \begin{pmatrix}2&2\7&-39\end{pmatrix}

