The only way for the product of six rolls to be odd is if all six rolls are odd.
The probability of rolling an odd number on a fair die is $\frac{1}{2}$, so the probability of rolling an odd number on each of six rolls is $\left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^6=\boxed{\frac{1}{64}}$.
The answer is: \frac{1}{64}

